# Provider stand-ins (ADR-0012): steer IDNow and World-Check at runtime, without code changes or restarts.

@stubs = http://127.0.0.1:5300

### All rules: configured (src/ProviderStubs/Atlas.ProviderStubs/appsettings.json) and runtime
GET {{stubs}}/_control/rules

### World-Check cases (possible matches waiting for an officer)
# @name cases
GET {{stubs}}/_control/cases

### Play the compliance officer: resolve the most recent case. outcome: CLEARED | CONFIRMED
POST {{stubs}}/_control/cases/{{cases.response.body.$[0].caseId}}/resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "outcome": "CLEARED", "officerId": "officer-mb-7" }

### "Recover" IDNow for documents marked idnow:DOWN (a runtime rule overrides the configured one)
POST {{stubs}}/_control/rules/idnow
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "idnow-recovered", "match": "idnow:DOWN" }

### Make World-Check slow for everyone (beyond the 10s attempt timeout): exercises timeouts and retries
POST {{stubs}}/_control/rules/worldcheck
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "wc-slow", "match": " ", "latencyMs": 12000 }

### Make IDNow return 429 twice for a marker, then answer normally
POST {{stubs}}/_control/rules/idnow
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "idnow-throttled", "match": "idnow:THROTTLED", "failTimes": 2, "failStatusCode": 429 }

### Remove all runtime rules and reset failure counters
DELETE {{stubs}}/_control/rules
